    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Detailed diagnosis of Armenian police educational system is implemented and final report with key findings and recommendations is developed.
2. New curricula for selected subjects and learning modules are developed.
3. ToT for Police Educational Complex lecturers are conducted.
4. Data and business processes mapping for the Police is implemented. Big data analytical tool for the Police Operational Management System is developed and tested. 
8. Police digital transformation roadmap is developed.
9. Gender Seal methodology application in the Police is implemented.
10. Capacity building in gender equality in Police is conducted.
12. The concept of DRR and CM in police is developed and gap analysis is implemented, relevant SoPs are developed.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Functional review of the Police Education Complex conducted during December 2021, with key recommendations for improvement provided. 
2. New curricula developed for the modules on &#x201c;Leadership and management; Human and Logistic Resources Management; IT for Law Enforcement Bodies; ToT for Law Enforcement Lecturers&#x201d;.
3. ToT for selected lecturers conducted on the Project developed learning modules.
4. A detailed data and business processes mapping of the police structures conducted that put the basis for development of the analytical platform.
8. The development of the roadmap is underway.
9. Gender Equality Seal Award methodology was launched to accelerate transformation for gender equality.
10. Training on &#x201c;Raising awareness on gender equality and gender based discrimination in police&#x201c; conducted for senior and middle rank officers.
12. A desk review of normative legal and internal acts regulating the police activities during crisis situations conducted and Disaster Risk Management framework applicable for the Police introduced.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
